# Answer Key

**Q1 — C.** 짠하다 means "to be pitiful / heartbreaking." Option B is a common trap — 짜다 means salty, but 짠하다 carries an emotional, sympathetic nuance.

**Q2 — B.** Hwasa said 고추잠자리 is the song she's been into (꽂힌 노래) recently.

**Q3 — C.** 멍청이. She playfully called her late-night viewers 멍청이들 (fools/idiots) for being awake so late.

**Q4 — B.** 자막 = sous-titres. Option A (doublage) is the translation for 더빙.

**Q5 — B.** 단종되다 means "to be discontinued." 단절되다 means "to be severed/cut off" and 단축되다 means "to be shortened" — both are plausible but incorrect.

**Q6 — B.** She said "나는 사실 더빙을 좋아해" — she prefers dubbing for animated content, linked to childhood nostalgia.

**Q7 — C.** 늘어나다 means "to stretch out / get loose." She was talking about a shirt that stretches out quickly.

**Q8 — C.** 귀엽다 = être mignon(ne). Options A and D (beau/joli) describe beauty rather than cuteness.

**Q9 — C.** 더빙 (dubbing). She was explaining she prefers dubbed versions of animated content.

**Q10 — C.** 향수 means nostalgia (in this context). 향기 = fragrance/scent, 향신료 = spice, 향상 = improvement.

**Q11 — B.** She was worried her favorite T-shirt would be discontinued (단종될까 봐). The stain topic came up separately.

**Q12 — C.** In this context, 꽂히다 means "to be hooked on / really into something." Its literal meaning involves being stuck/stabbed, but here it's used figuratively.

**Q13 — B.** 걱정하다 = s'inquiéter. Option A (se fâcher) means "to get angry."

**Q14 — C.** 얼룩 = stain. 얼굴 = face, 얼음 = ice, 얼핏 = at a glance — all visually similar but entirely different words.

**Q15 — B.** She was asking fans whether they should feel excited (설레다) or worried (걱정하다).

**Q16 — B.** 명곡 = a famous song / masterpiece song (명 = renowned + 곡 = song).

**Q17 — C.** 편해 (comfortable). She was showing off her outfit and commenting on how comfortable it looks.

**Q18 — B.** 변신하다 = se transformer. Option A (se déguiser) means "to disguise oneself," which implies hiding identity rather than transformation.

**Q19 — B.** She mentioned having long hair (장발) for years and expressed interest in trying various short hairstyles (단발).

**Q20 — B.** 지겹다 = to be bored / sick of. 지치다 means "to be exhausted" and 지루하다 also means "to be boring" but is a different word. The transcript specifically uses 지겹다.

**Q21 — C.** 울다 = pleurer. Option A (crier) means "to shout" in French — a classic false friend for English speakers.

**Q22 — B.** 빨려 들어가다 = to be sucked in / drawn in / absorbed. Hwasa used it to describe being completely absorbed into a scene.

**Q23 — B.** She said she cried a lot at the end (마지막에 엄청 울었잖아) when family-related storylines came up (가족 얘기 나오면서).

**Q24 — B.** 얼룩 (stain). She was asking how many food stains it takes before you throw out a piece of clothing.

**Q25 — C.** 가족 = famille.

**Q26 — C.** 감명 = deep impression. 감동 (being moved/touched) is close but distinct. 감정 = emotion, 감각 = sense/sensation.

**Q27 — B.** 멍청이들 (idiots/fools). She used it as a playful, affectionate nickname for fans staying up late.

**Q28 — B.** 단발 = short hair / bob cut. While 단발 can literally mean "single shot" in other contexts, in this transcript it refers exclusively to a hairstyle.

**Q29 — C.** 명곡 (masterpiece song). She said 고추잠자리 was already a 명곡 but it really hit her emotionally (가슴에 팍 꽂히더라).

**Q30 — B.** In context, 향수 meant nostalgia — watching dubbed cartoons triggers childhood memories for her. 향수 can also mean "perfume," but the context makes the meaning clear.
